      "description": "Watch Lens vs Paris Saint Germain highlights and goals from Coupe de France on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 16, 2026. The CAF Super Cup delivered a high-stakes thriller on August 16, 2026 , as two tactical heavyweights clashed in a match defined by narrow margins and disciplinary drama. The atmosphere was electric as both sides fought for continental glory in a game that swung unpredictably from start to finish. Thauvin Strikes Before Disciplinary Chaos While Paris Saint-Germain controlled the early tempo, it was Lens who found the breakthrough against the run of play. In the 32nd minute, Matthieu Udol turned provider, setting up Florian Thauvin to fire home with his right foot. The joy for the Lens faithful was short-lived, however, as the match took a dramatic turn in the 39th minute. Kyllian Antonio was shown a straight red card for a serious foul, forcing his team into a defensive shell for the remainder of the contest. The tension boiled over to the sidelines, where Dino Toppmoeller received a yellow card for his vocal protests. PSG looked to capitalize immediately, and they came agonizingly close just before the break. Desire Doue beat the keeper but saw his effort crash against the post in stoppage time. Despite the numerical disadvantage, Lens held firm to take a slim lead into the interval. VAR Drama and a Frantic Finish The second half saw a relentless PSG siege, bolstered by a triple substitution in the 60th minute that introduced Ousmane Dembele , Fabian Ruiz , and Nuno Mendes . The pressure appeared to have paid off in the 76th minute when the ball found the net, but a lengthy VAR check eventually ruled the goal out for an offside against Desire Doue . Despite boasting 69% possession, the Parisian giants struggled to break down a resolute Lens backline led by the heroics of their defensive unit. As the clock ticked toward full-time, the game descended into chaos. In the 86th minute, the numbers were leveled when Nuno Mendes was sent off following heavy protests. The final moments were punctuated by a flurry of yellow cards for Achraf Hakimi and Fabian Ruiz as tempers flared. Ultimately, in front of a crowd of 38,223, Lens survived late scares from Dembele to secure a famous victory and lift the trophy."
